OL,3,AChancellor rejects calls to raise
OL,4,ACapital Gains Tax in Budget
OL,5,
OL,6,FChancellor John Healey has dismissed
OL,7,Fcalls from some Labour MPs to increase
OL,8,FCapital Gains Tax (CGT).
OL,10,FCabinet ministers Wes Streeting and
OL,11,FLouise Haigh both previously voiced
OL,12,Fsupport for raising CGT before Andy
OL,13,FBurnham became prime minister in July.
OL,15,FAhead of next week's Budget, as first
OL,16,Freported by the Times, Healey is minded
OL,17,Fnot to increase CGT - which is imposed
OL,18,Fon the profit people make when they
OL,19,Fsell an asset that has increased in
OL,20,Fvalue, such as shares in a company or
OL,21,Fproperties which are not primary
OL,22,Fresidences.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
